{"kind":"report","text":"Exact-head review of 56eb23168178d951d0486fc62e91162f7d6b688e, resting on all nine artifacts, docs/protocol.md first. Changes requested.\n\nArchitecture: conditions 1–4 are substantially addressed. Carry is a policy-version-bound sealed judgment, with both positive and negative outcomes; policy activation invalidates it. Runner identity is a current configuration pin, with a separately measured service result, rather than the earlier check's value. Unpinned checks cannot carry. Snapshot identity, time, parentlessness, message and digest are reproducible, and filtered CheckBody.integration consistently names the snapshot bound by the Room to the canonical integration. Jobs have a stated trusted service-binding boundary, base, volatile/advisory flags and exact gitAuthEnv shape. The required edits correctly distinguish contract types from the unmerged A/G implementations and call out L's decoder before the new event is emitted.\n\nP2 — restrict a filtered job's reads to its current snapshot object set (docs/protocol.md:2481–2484 with R-EXEC-9). R-CARRY-15 stores successive snapshot commits in the Room's per-checker snapshot repository, while the job receives read authority for that repository. Parentless commits and a fresh checkout prevent inherited canonical history, but do not prevent fetching another retained snapshot ref from the same readable repository. An older snapshot can expose a file absent from this job's snapshot, for example after a checker input changes or a file is deleted. This contradicts R-CARRY-9's requirement that the runner can see nothing beyond its filtered snapshot and R-EXEC-7's omitted-object isolation.\n\nIndependent local Git reproduction: two parentless commits with the specified fixed identity/message and correct SHA-256 digests of their [path,mode,blob] arrays were published at refs/artroom/snapshots/\u003cdigest\u003e in one repository. A new runner fetched and checked out the current empty snapshot, then, using only the same repository read access, fetched the older snapshot ref and read its omitted file. Current commit bed5a06e24f68aef8e268db6f0d9ed080e787c93; older commit 26537b6dfe93f8d43e8a39471b6a9c2c03aa2102. Fixture and results are recorded in /tmp/artroom-checker-amend3-isolation.json. This is a Git capability model reproduction, not a deployed Artifacts/token test. It demonstrates why the contract's repository-wide read boundary is insufficient unless an additional current-object restriction is required.\n\nAmend the storage/read rules so a job can fetch only the closure of its recorded snapshot: a repository containing only that snapshot, or an enforced per-job read capability/gateway restricted to the exact objects. Do not rely on checkout, parentlessness, undisclosed old IDs, removing refs without an object-access proof, or merely disabling carry. Preserve snapshot reuse where it can meet isolation. Add normative cases for an omitted file in an older snapshot, both known-SHA and advertised-ref fetches, concurrent jobs, and configuration changes, alongside exact current commit fetch success. Route the resulting requirement to A/G/B.\n\nSecurity: the configured service binding is a capability boundary, not proof of a job signature or a particular caller's Room identity. Cloudflare documents account-local explicit service bindings and RPC capability visibility (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/service-bindings/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/rpc/visibility/). Restrict deployment bindings to trusted Room producers and exclude the harness job-building HTTP route as the amendment requires. Nonblocking wording correction: the claim that any forged job can only produce a Room-refused check is broader than the stated checks prove; a bound trusted caller could submit a job with valid recorded bindings. State the operator trust boundary rather than that unconditional guarantee. Volatile equality in both directions, pinned runner comparison before code, private signing and exact snapshot ID confirmation are sound.\n\nSimplification: one deterministic snapshot serialization and one explicit job contract remove the A/G mismatch. Keep one current-object access boundary; do not add incidental checks at checkout while leaving repository-wide authority. The two jj decisions are explicitly open as condition 5 permits. This does not withdraw the planned complete per-change history functionality or turn current absence into product completion.\n\nValidation: root strict typecheck and every package's npm test passed: Git 118 Node, log 100 Node/95 workerd, policy 190 Node/189 workerd with its existing one skip, and UI 88. The compiled check-job example and new checker configuration validation test pass. All nine changed artifacts were read fully against the specified main base 0ad67937; the isolated source worktree is clean. No source implementation was changed by checker, and no deployment, external token operation or network Git mutation was performed. Runtime A/G/L adoption, carry replay and actual production end-to-end admission remain required lane work, not proven by these contract checks.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:14f305cb0052c21d037a3a82b95ec0dfaa72b6c9","binding":"assigned","head":"56eb23168178d951d0486fc62e91162f7d6b688e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:33b8abf50d5018166448d3420a61b2a26ef01359\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c77b3003ce0ad6003894e3452cf3c2aa1a7584b2\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:33b8abf50d5018166448d3420a61b2a26ef01359","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}